# .htaccess for the veryklear.com site on SiteGround (the bare domain).
# Sends every request to the same path on www, which Railway serves:
# veryklear.com/strategiesessie -> https://www.veryklear.com/strategiesessie
# The query string is kept. Replaces the Domain -> Redirects rule, which
# dropped the path. Upload by hand; see DEPLOY.md.

# Security headers on the redirect itself. The bare domain serves no page, only
# this 301, but scanners judge the response they get. The real site's headers
# come from the Express server (server/app.ts).
# No Referrer-Policy here, on purpose: a browser applies the policy of a redirect
# response to the request it follows, so even "no-referrer" would strip the
# referrer before it reaches www and LinkedIn or Google visits would count as direct.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header always set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
  Header always set Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'"
  Header always set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
  Header always set X-Frame-Options "DENY"
</IfModule>

RewriteEngine On
RewriteCond %{HTTP_HOST} ^veryklear\.com$ [NC]
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://www.veryklear.com/$1 [R=301,L]
